-          "quote": "Let $A\\in F^{n\\times n}$ be Hurwitz, let $B\\in F^{n\\times r}$, and let $p_1,\\ldots,p_k\\in\\mathbb C$ be a finite shift list. The target equation is $AX+XA^*+BB^*=0$. Inputs also include the shift list and exact linear-solve operations. For real $A,B$, every nonreal shift must be immediately followed by its complex conjugate; the procedure may use complex arithmetic for these paired shifts.\n\nInitialize $R_0=B$, let $Z_0$ have zero columns, and set $X_0=0$. For $j=1,\\ldots,k$:\n\n1. If, for real data, a nonreal shift is not immediately followed by its conjugate, return `unpaired-complex-shift`. If $\\operatorname{Re}p_j\\ge0$, return `invalid-shift`. If $A+p_jI$ is singular, return `singular-shift`.\n2. Set $c_j=-2\\operatorname{Re}p_j>0$ and solve\n   $$\n   V_j=(A+p_jI)^{-1}R_{j-1}.\n   $$\n3. Set\n   $$\n   Z_j=[Z_{j-1},\\sqrt{c_j}V_j],\\qquad X_j=Z_jZ_j^*=X_{j-1}+c_jV_jV_j^*,\\qquad R_j=R_{j-1}+c_jV_j.\n   $$\n\nReturn `completed` with the low-rank factor $Z_k$, approximation $X_k$, and residual factor $R_k$. A finite shift list may stop before convergence; this procedure does not select shifts or assert unconditional convergence.\n\n",
+          "quote": "Let $A\\in F^{n\\times n}$ be Hurwitz, let $B\\in F^{n\\times r}$, and let $p_1,\\ldots,p_k\\in\\mathbb C$ be a finite shift list. The target equation is $AX+XA^*+BB^*=0$. Inputs also include the shift list and exact linear-solve operations. For real $A,B$, nonreal shifts must occur in consecutive complex-conjugate pairs; the procedure may use complex arithmetic for these paired shifts.\n\nBefore starting matrix updates, validate the real-data shift pairing by scanning the shift list once: at a real shift advance the scan index by one; at a nonreal shift require the next list entry to equal its complex conjugate, then advance the scan index by two. A missing or unequal partner returns `unpaired-complex-shift`. For complex data no pairing restriction is imposed. This validation scan consumes pairs; the update loop below still processes every individual shift in order.\n\nInitialize $R_0=B$, let $Z_0$ have zero columns, and set $X_0=0$. For $j=1,\\ldots,k$:\n\n1. If $\\operatorname{Re}p_j\\ge0$, return `invalid-shift`. If $A+p_jI$ is singular, return `singular-shift`.\n2. Set $c_j=-2\\operatorname{Re}p_j>0$ and solve\n   $$\n   V_j=(A+p_jI)^{-1}R_{j-1}.\n   $$\n3. Set\n   $$\n   Z_j=[Z_{j-1},\\sqrt{c_j}V_j],\\qquad X_j=Z_jZ_j^*=X_{j-1}+c_jV_jV_j^*,\\qquad R_j=R_{j-1}+c_jV_j.\n   $$\n\nReturn `completed` with the low-rank factor $Z_k$, approximation $X_k$, and residual factor $R_k$. A finite shift list may stop before convergence; this procedure does not select shifts or assert unconditional convergence.",
